Given, \[\iint_S 5\vec{r}\cdot \hat{n}\,ds\] Using Divergence theorem, \[\iint_S \vec{A}\cdot \hat{n}\,ds
=
\iiint_V (\nabla \cdot \vec{A})\,dv\] Here, \[\vec{A}=5\vec{r}
=
5(x\hat{a}_x+y\hat{a}_y+z\hat{a}_z)\] Therefore, \[\nabla \cdot \vec{A}
=
\frac{\partial (5x)}{\partial x}
+
\frac{\partial (5y)}{\partial y}
+
\frac{\partial (5z)}{\partial z}\] \[=5+5+5=15\] Hence, \[\iint_S 5\vec{r}\cdot \hat{n}\,ds
=
\iiint_V 15\,dv\] \[=15V\] \[\boxed{\text{(d) }15V}\]

